      "prompt": "In an isosceles trapezoid $ABCD$, the parallel bases are $AB = 6$ and $CD = 16$, and the non-parallel legs are $AD = BC = 13$. Diagonals $AC$ and $BD$ intersect at point $E$. Find the exact area of lower triangle $CDE$.",
      "display": "\\text{Trapezoid } ABCD:\\ AB = 6,\\ CD = 16,\\ AD = BC = 13 \\implies \\text{Area}(\\triangle CDE) = ?",
      "plainText": "(1/2) * 16 * sqrt(13^2 - ((16 - 6)/2)^2) * (16/(6 + 16))",
